# Wireframe: Layout Module — Responsive Sidebar & Theme Control

## Purpose & Flow Context

This wireframe defines the responsive layout structure for the Linear App Clone, supporting desktop, tablet, and mobile experiences with theme switching capability. The layout module serves as the primary navigation framework across all screens, enabling users to access projects, tasks, and settings while maintaining consistent sidebar and theme states.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |
| `[☰]` | Hamburger menu (mobile) | `[←]` | Back button |
| `[...]` | Theme toggle control | `[...]` | Sidebar toggle |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm intent.

**App-shell**: Shared header + nav + container. Regions:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Logo, app title, user menu, theme toggle | Fixed top, 64px height |
| Sidebar | Navigation links, logo, user settings | Left side, 240px expanded, 64px collapsed |
| Main Content | Primary content area | Flexible width, max 1440px |
| Footer | App info, version | Optional, bottom |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Primary content area (main tasks/data)
2. Sidebar navigation (access to sections)
3. Header controls (theme, user settings)

