## Components & Affordances

### Header Components

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Logo | Image/Text | Click → Dashboard | Fallback to text if image fails |
| App Title | Text (heading-3) | Click → Dashboard | — |
| Theme Toggle | ThemeToggle | Click → Cycle themes (light/dark/system) | Shows current state |
| User Menu | Button + Dropdown | Click → User settings dropdown | — |
| Hamburger Menu (mobile) | Button | Click → Open sidebar overlay | Only on mobile/tablet |

### Sidebar Components

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Sidebar Container | Sidebar | Desktop: expanded/collapsed, Mobile: overlay | Responsive breakpoints |
| Navigation Items | Button/Link | Click → Navigate to section | Active state highlighting |
| Toggle Button | Button | Click → Expand/collapse sidebar | Desktop/tablet only |
| Close Button (mobile) | Button | Click → Close sidebar overlay | Only on mobile |
| Backdrop (mobile) | Overlay | Click → Close sidebar overlay | Only on mobile |

### Main Content Components

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Page Title | Text (heading-1) | Display current section title | — |
| Content Area | Container | Flexible layout based on section | Loading/skeleton states |

---

## Data Display

The layout module itself doesn't display data—it provides the navigation framework. Data display patterns are defined per-section (Projects, Tasks, Settings).

**Navigation State Management**:
- Sidebar state persists across page refreshes (expanded/collapsed)
- Active navigation item highlights current section
- Theme preference persists in local storage

---

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| App Title | "Linear App Clone" - brand identifier | Consistent across all screens |
| Navigation Items | Section names: Dashboard, Projects, Tasks, Settings | Clear, action-oriented labels |
| Theme Toggle | "Theme" - user preference control | Shows current state (Light/Dark/System) |
| Hamburger Menu | "Menu" - navigation access on mobile | Icon-only with aria-label |
| Close Button | "Close" - dismiss sidebar overlay | Icon-only with aria-label |

---

## States

### Populated (Default)

The layout displays with:
- Header with logo, title, theme toggle, and user menu
- Sidebar with navigation items (expanded on desktop, collapsed on tablet, hidden on mobile)
- Main content area displaying current section content
- Active navigation item highlighted

### Empty

Not applicable—layout module is always populated with navigation structure.

### Loading

Skeleton layout mirrors the populated structure:

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [===== skeleton bar =====]   [==== skeleton ===]               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [==== skeleton bar =====]                                       |
|  [==== skeleton bar =====]                                       |
|  [==== skeleton bar =====]                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Error

Not applicable—layout module doesn't load data. If navigation fails, display error message in main content area.

### Success / Confirmation

Not applicable—layout module is structural, not transactional.

---

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Sidebar always visible (expanded), full header controls |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Sidebar collapsible (toggle button), header controls stack |
| Mobile (<768px) | Sidebar hidden (hamburger menu), header controls minimal |

**Responsive Behaviors**:
- Sidebar collapses automatically when viewport shrinks below 1024px
- Sidebar expands automatically when viewport grows above 1024px
- Mobile sidebar opens as overlay with backdrop
- Theme toggle remains accessible at all breakpoints
- Touch targets ≥24×24 CSS px on mobile

---

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | header, nav (sidebar), main, complementary |
| Heading order | h1 → h2 → h3 — one h1 per screen |
| Reading / Focus order | Header → Sidebar → Main content (top→bottom, left→right) |
| Accessible names | Hamburger menu: "Open navigation menu", Close button: "Close navigation menu" |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through header → sidebar → main, Enter/Space for selections, Escape closes mobile sidebar |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation on all interactive targets |
| Focus not obscured | Sidebar toggle button always visible, header fixed but not obscuring focus |
| Non-color intent | Active navigation: icon + text + background highlight, never color alone |

**Screen Reader Support**:
- Sidebar: "Navigation" landmark with accessible name "Main navigation"
- Theme toggle: "Theme selector, current theme: [light/dark/system]"
- Hamburger menu: "Open navigation menu"
- Close button: "Close navigation menu"
- Active item: "Current page: [section name]"

---

## Component Reference

This wireframe uses the following design-system components:

| Component | Usage | Variant |
|-----------|-------|---------|
| Button | Sidebar toggle, hamburger menu, close button | primary, secondary |
| Sidebar | Navigation panel | desktop, tablet, mobile |
| ThemeToggle | Theme selection control | button, dropdown |
| Modal | Not used in layout module | — |

**Deferred to Design System**:
- Exact color contrast ratios
- Focus appearance styling
- Component-specific target sizes
- Pixel-perfect spacing values